Subject: [PATCH] [M156] Swap event_queue_ before filtering in DispatchEvents

FlyWeb next batch: from branch-heads/8078 5d427d384f. Applied after seguridad/siguiente/chromium/0007; applies cleanly (identical diff). No brave-core patches or chromium_src for these files.

Original change's description:
> Swap event_queue_ before filtering in DispatchEvents
>
> When ScriptedAnimationController::DispatchEvents is called with a
> filter, it previously iterated directly over event_queue_ while
> invoking filter.Run(event). If the filter callback synchronously
> triggers script execution (for example, page_reveal_event_filter
> calling ResolveCrossDocumentViewTransition(), which skips a
> cross-document transition and advances a captured element-scoped view
> transition to its DOM update callback) and that script enqueues new
> events into event_queue_, event_queue_ can reallocate its backing
> buffer while DispatchEvents is still iterating over it.
>
> Swap event_queue_ into a local HeapVector before running the filter
> loop, and append any newly enqueued events to the remaining
> un-dispatched events afterward.
>
